<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Transportation Line">
  <data key="d0">Transportation Line</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A system of roads designated as official routes, requiring specific facilities and protection to be considered a valid true transportation line.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Home Country">
  <data key="d0">Home Country</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Home Country refers to the nation where an army originates, where base switching consumes time and limits operational freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;The domestic territory of the forces, where movement is flexible and local government assistance is available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77045b1c2599a8ac0acb0e781562ae49</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Country">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Country</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy Country refers to hostile territory where supply storage requires fortresses and border facilities are often lacking.&lt;SEP&gt;Foreign territory where troop movement is restricted to specific fortified lines and lacks local support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77045b1c2599a8ac0acb0e781562ae49</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troops">
  <data key="d0">Troops</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Troops represent military units seeking sustenance through various methods depending on time constraints and environmental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Military units whose operational mobility depends on the distinction between operating at home or abroad.&lt;SEP&gt;Troops denote military units that require secure retreat paths and effective command structures to avoid encirclement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6ca1393bac88b8acf9da2a729f68294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e30125fa729c9d2fb7970405171875</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Body Forces">
  <data key="d0">Main Body Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Large military formations that are significantly constrained by the need to maintain secure supply lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Garrison Forces">
  <data key="d0">Garrison Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Smaller units stationed to support and maintain the security of the transportation lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supply Depots">
  <data key="d0">Supply Depots</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Warehouses established along transport lines that contribute to the classification of the road as a true transportation line.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hospitals">
  <data key="d0">Hospitals</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical facilities required along transport lines to validate their status as official arteries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supply Stations">
  <data key="d0">Supply Stations</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Logistic posts assigned to support the army along the transportation routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rivers">
  <data key="d0">Rivers</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Rivers served as barriers behind camps to provide security for troops encamped in earlier times.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural waterways that serve as critical components influencing the choice of transport routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2918db8fd4527a62709762ff6d5e2b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bridges">
  <data key="d0">Bridges</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Structures crossing rivers that act as key transit points determining transport line suitability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supply System">
  <data key="d0">Supply System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Supply System is a specialized制度for army provisioning involving storage, transport, and baking of food.&lt;SEP&gt;Supply System refers to the complex logistical framework involving food and material transport required for military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The logistical method used for feeding armies, determining the effectiveness of disrupting enemy lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6ca1393bac88b8acf9da2a729f68294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c8520f94840f0c06aabc2e77297761e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22b58faf893c88031c709a0cfac971fb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flanking Maneuver">
  <data key="d0">Flanking Maneuver</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Large-scale lateral movements executed to exploit open space and gain positional advantage over the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;Tactical operations aimed at harassing enemy lines or cutting off retreat paths.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e041dafef58e97722effb6d5aec49ec1</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Base">
  <data key="d0">Base</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Base is defined as large storage points representing the nation, crucial for sustaining the army and its movements.&lt;SEP&gt;The originating area from which forces operate, requiring connection via stable transportation lines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77045b1c2599a8ac0acb0e781562ae49</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commander">
  <data key="d0">Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The military leader responsible for directing forces where branch proportions are typically fixed.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual responsible for issuing orders and maintaining authority over military forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commander is the individual responsible for gaining situational awareness influenced by the physical positioning of the headquarters.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals responsible for designating security personnel and controlling transport line responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commander leads troops but experiences reduced influence on battle outcomes when terrain forces dispersed action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e041dafef58e97722effb6d5aec49ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb948420cdd6d2bd78179f476f0df5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93ec7c5511e20868c576f5b6c5fefe41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d696492803499031b7e887c1814ba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6725d3545cdb40e1dfdd2209aba40f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Military Police">
  <data key="d0">Military Police</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Security detachments dispatched to guard and police the assigned roads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post Office">
  <data key="d0">Post Office</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Communication facilities required to establish a road as a definitive transportation line.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Administrative Organs">
  <data key="d0">Administrative Organs</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Government-like institutions established by the army to enforce authority in enemy territory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Population">
  <data key="d0">Local Population</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The civilian inhabitants of the region where military operations occur, whose perception and resistance significantly impact troop security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flour Carts">
  <data key="d0">Flour Carts</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Logistical vehicles used for bulk supply transport, representing the material scale of the feeding system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retreat Path">
  <data key="d0">Retreat Path</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific routes used for withdrawing troops, distinguished from standard transportation lines used for advance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quartermasters">
  <data key="d0">Quartermasters</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Military officers assigned to manage supply and logistical coordination within the command structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wing Side Action">
  <data key="d0">Wing Side Action</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific tactical maneuvers targeting the enemy's flanks to cause decisive disruption or strikes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resistance involves actively fighting enemy forces to create time while minimizing risk of encirclement.&lt;SEP&gt;Active fighting undertaken by outlying forces to hinder the enemy and gain strategic time.&lt;SEP&gt;Active opposition by local populations against military presence and infrastructure establishment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5bb89666881fe685b53314cebe1abaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b9839be4f5c76a97ace71baf8a2625</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Material Advantages">
  <data key="d0">Material Advantages</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tangible resources and physical assets that provide strategic superiority in conflict.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spiritual Advantages">
  <data key="d0">Spiritual Advantages</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychological or morale-related strengths that contribute to combat effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f2cc24375db4a5ea1a5780368f5b39f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Templehof">
  <data key="d0">Templehof</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Templehof is a translator whose work on the history of the Seven Years' War provides insights into marching deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History of the Seven Years' War">
  <data key="d0">History of the Seven Years' War</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The History of the Seven Years' War is a text cited for understanding historical marching constraints and deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Division">
  <data key="d0">Standard Division</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A typical military unit comprising 8,000 to 10,000 personnel capable of fighting for several hours.&lt;SEP&gt;A Standard Division consists of approximately 8000 personnel including infantry, artillery, and vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modern Military Art">
  <data key="d0">Modern Military Art</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modern Military Art enables the organic subdivision of forces into smaller operational units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Road">
  <data key="d0">Main Road</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Main Roads are primary infrastructure used by artillery and heavy divisions during movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Path">
  <data key="d0">Small Path</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Small Paths are alternative routes found in agricultural zones to support smaller detachment movements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European Central Region">
  <data key="d0">European Central Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Central Region offers accessible small paths near main roads for military movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountainous Area">
  <data key="d0">Mountainous Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Mountainous Areas have fewer parallel roads, making route connections difficult but increasing resistance capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prussian Mile">
  <data key="d0">Prussian Mile</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A historical unit of distance measurement used to calculate the separation ranges between different military units.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prussian Mile is defined as equivalent to 7532.48 meters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prussian Mile serves as a unit of measurement for defining distances in military marching formations.&lt;SEP&gt;Prussian Mile is the unit of measurement used to describe distances between military positions and camps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f00c9046ba6740391ca82c677577b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfddc40b68714749a17f1f73f04abea</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774681</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Readiness">
  <data key="d0">Combat Readiness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Readiness is the state required when operating near enemies to ensure immediate defense.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat readiness is directly impacted by the availability of food and the morale derived from adequate provisioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2a90ee6c570c1f41213848bde0e55e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8b814c286eb1e073648265d5177eb69</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marching Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Marching Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Marching Deployment dictates how troops organize into columns and skirmisher lines during movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troop Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Troop Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Troop Concentration refers to gathering divided forces together before engaging in battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Troop Concentration focuses on gathering forces together, which may be avoided in complex terrain due to risks and limitations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb948420cdd6d2bd78179f476f0df5a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Forces">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The opposing military units engaging the main force, capable of attacking and capturing specialized equipment.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing military group capable of threatening the Main Body by attacking the Flanks or controlling superior supply lines.&lt;SEP&gt;The opposing army attempting to surround and attack the outlying force.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy Forces represent the opposing threat near which troops must maintain constant combat readiness.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy Forces represent the threat that compels the army to maintain constant vigilance and logistical readiness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e041dafef58e97722effb6d5aec49ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5bb89666881fe685b53314cebe1abaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c8520f94840f0c06aabc2e77297761e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skirmisher Line">
  <data key="d0">Skirmisher Line</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skirmisher Lines are dispersed infantry formations used when protecting artillery or moving through terrain obstacles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cavalry Reserve">
  <data key="d0">Cavalry Reserve</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cavalry Reserve acts as a mobile support element within larger force structures such as 4 Infantry Divisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artillery Reserve">
  <data key="d0">Artillery Reserve</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Artillery Reserve comprises heavy units whose movement length is calculated as 1 hour travel time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Travel Time">
  <data key="d0">Standard Travel Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard Travel Time represents the duration (1 hour) equivalent to the physical road occupation of a standard division.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agricultural Zone">
  <data key="d0">Agricultural Zone</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Agricultural Zones are regions containing parallel small paths that facilitate military bypasses around main roads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troop Separation Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Troop Separation Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Troop Separation Ratio describes the inverse mathematical relationship between the amount of divided force and independent action time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68695250ec43f3b423a5df5d30602c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle of Borodino">
  <data key="d0">Battle of Borodino</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Battle of Borodino was a confrontation between the French and Russian armies characterized by equal forces and simple power competition.&lt;SEP&gt;A significant engagement within the 1812 Campaign where Pyotr Ivanovich Bagration was killed.&lt;SEP&gt;A major decisive battle in the 1812 campaign where French losses reached 144,000 including killed and wounded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c55a94307c751d0e9fbf6270e7773d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6e328b37fa2162a0fbd3f638331548</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dresden Battle">
  <data key="d0">Dresden Battle</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Dresden Battle in 1813 is cited as a notable exception where Napoleon achieved a victory under specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dresden Battle was a conflict where Napoleon won with smaller numbers against a larger enemy force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leipzig Battle">
  <data key="d0">Leipzig Battle</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Leipzig Battle is a specific conflict where Napoleon failed due to insufficient concentration of forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Leipzig Battle was a conflict where Napoleon lost despite having a large force against the Coalition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brienne Battle">
  <data key="d0">Brienne Battle</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brienne Battle is listed as a failure for Napoleon resulting from an inability to maintain sufficient force advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Brienne Battle was a conflict resulting in defeat for Napoleon's forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laon Battle">
  <data key="d0">Laon Battle</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Laon Battle is another instance where Napoleon encountered defeat under similar strategic limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Laon Battle was a conflict resulting in defeat for Napoleon's forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Propitious Match Battle">
  <data key="d0">Propitious Match Battle</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Propitious Match Battle is referenced as another engagement where Napoleon did not succeed due to force imbalance issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Troop Strength">
  <data key="d0">Troop Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Troop Strength refers to the numerical comparison of opposing forces, serving as a decisive factor when combat factors are balanced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morale">
  <data key="d0">Morale</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Morale represents the courage and spiritual strength of the army, capable of multiplying physical power.&lt;SEP&gt;Morale represents the psychological state and fighting spirit of troops, critically influencing outcomes in dispersed combat formations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb948420cdd6d2bd78179f476f0df5a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commander Talent">
  <data key="d0">Commander Talent</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Commander Talent describes the ability of high-level commanders which becomes critical when troop strength is nearly equal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Experience">
  <data key="d0">Combat Experience</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat Experience is cited as a significant advantage for armies that cannot differentiate through technology or training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Military Art">
  <data key="d0">Military Art</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Military Art refers to the pursuit of utilizing terrain cleverly according to comprehensive principles.&lt;SEP&gt;Military Art refers to the principles and methods of conducting warfare and strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;The evolving field of warfare strategies and doctrines, characterized by changes starting from decisive actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The discipline discussed in the text where camp quarters are considered necessary for modern military forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-942da2473ae7c7645f080c44aba00371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2918db8fd4527a62709762ff6d5e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6e328b37fa2162a0fbd3f638331548</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="War Theory">
  <data key="d0">War Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">War Theory refers to strategic principles governing force allocation and engagement effectiveness that face limitations under uneven force conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weapons and Equipment">
  <data key="d0">Weapons and Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Weapons and Equipment refer to military hardware where modern armies have achieved significant parity in organization and training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Terrain is considered a critical factor in military operations, likened to a fundamental book for commanders.&lt;SEP&gt;Terrain represents geographical features historically utilized in military art, though reliance on complex terrain usage has declined.&lt;SEP&gt;Geographic features that influence the duration and safety of resistance and retreat operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-942da2473ae7c7645f080c44aba00371&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5bb89666881fe685b53314cebe1abaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8b814c286eb1e073648265d5177eb69</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Political Decision">
  <data key="d0">Political Decision</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Political Decision involves arbitrary government choices that determine whether war occurs regardless of force disparities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="War Purpose">
  <data key="d0">War Purpose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">War Purpose denotes the objectives set for a conflict, which should scale proportionally with available troop strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="War Duration">
  <data key="d0">War Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">War Duration signifies the length of time a conflict lasts, expected to shorten as troop strength decreases to limit risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22b58faf893c88031c709a0cfac971fb</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strategic Balance">
  <data key="d0">Strategic Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strategic Balance describes the equilibrium state where combat skills and training equalize, making troop strength the deciding factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f1e8fe38b90ff6dffdb7380ea9e159d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legion">
  <data key="d0">Legion</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Legion is a large strategic unit that should ideally be divided into two or three corps or divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A large military unit divided into multiple subordinate parts such as corps and divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A large military formation consisting of approximately 200,000 personnel, subject to specific organizational division theories.&lt;SEP&gt;A Legion represents a large-scale military unit subject to specific deployment and strategic support considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;A large military unit composed of multiple divisions or corps, mentioned in structural contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2918db8fd4527a62709762ff6d5e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-089e96fcb6c53d4fe37413f70873aedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93ec7c5511e20868c576f5b6c5fefe41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-223fc84be8831740cffa7582ec0ee05a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corps">
  <data key="d0">Corps</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Corps consists of combat personnel in the same theater under a single supreme commander or retaining a traditional name.&lt;SEP&gt;Corps represents a subdivision of a Legion alongside divisions in the strategic organization of forces.&lt;SEP&gt;An intermediate military formation within a legion, typically comprising multiple divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;An intermediate military unit level situated between the Legion and Division, influencing command flexibility.&lt;SEP&gt;A larger military command structure consisting of 3 to 4 Divisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A sub-unit of a legion, equivalent to divisions in other organizational structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Corps represent a tier in the fighting sequence hierarchy where geometric changes occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2918db8fd4527a62709762ff6d5e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93ec7c5511e20868c576f5b6c5fefe41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9577d681c513d8a72e8f9e09ad316f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-223fc84be8831740cffa7582ec0ee05a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a0950d107000f63848660e8ffc0706</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical military unit generally consisting of 2000 to 5000 personnel.&lt;SEP&gt;A tactical unit composed of soldiers, forming the basic element of smaller military subdivisions with specific strength targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Brigades are components of the modern fighting sequence subject to organizational division.&lt;SEP&gt;A Brigade is a military unit whose battle entry timing became less critical under the new battle sequence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93ec7c5511e20868c576f5b6c5fefe41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38f13e59336c7bb333fab6bbbe0ac097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a0950d107000f63848660e8ffc0706</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command Hierarchy">
  <data key="d0">Command Hierarchy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The layered structure of command authority within a military unit, impacting operational speed and accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strategic Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Strategic Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The arrangement of military forces determined by strategic reasons rather than basic tactics.&lt;SEP&gt;The high-level positioning of forces determined by overall mission objectives rather than immediate battlefield conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93ec7c5511e20868c576f5b6c5fefe41</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774686</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The specific spatial arrangement of military units determined by immediate engagement requirements and battle specifics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle Order">
  <data key="d0">Battle Order</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The comprehensive arrangement combining the division and deployment of a force intended for imminent battle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774687</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined Arms">
  <data key="d0">Combined Arms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The integration of multiple military branches to maximize strength and cover tactical deficiencies inherent in individual branches.&lt;SEP&gt;The integration of different military branches, necessary for independent operation within larger units like Corps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1b2820cc1e95701eebf7342c4385d7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountain Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Mountain Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Mountain terrain presents significant obstacles that hinder the ability of a commander to effectively direct multiple divisions simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="River Obstacles">
  <data key="d0">River Obstacles</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Large rivers can physically bisect a Legion, making it impossible for a single commander to direct the separated sections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774688</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserves">
  <data key="d0">Reserves</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserves refer to manpower retained within military branches specifically for reinforcement or operational flexibility during engagements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command Efficiency Rules">
  <data key="d0">Command Efficiency Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Command Efficiency Rules establish the optimal number of subordinate parts a commander should manage to maintain order and flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Commanders are responsible for directing military formations, though their authority is limited by terrain and organizational structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders are leadership figures whose decisions significantly influence the safety of retreat routes.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders are leaders whose comparative qualities and competence are the primary factors in assessing military strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-58e69b3684e2bdfaee22cb77833e8174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6ca1393bac88b8acf9da2a729f68294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee5ef82512a6fb9049bd1bfe1863bb38</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774689</data>
