<node id="Separate Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Separate Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Separate Deployment is a military strategy involving the distribution of troops into independent parts based on specific purposes such as observation, reserves, and flank protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vanguard Force">
  <data key="d0">Vanguard Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical unit deployed forward to observe the enemy and delay their advance without engaging independently.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vanguard Force is an advanced unit deployed ahead of the main body to provide warning and defense against the enemy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserve Force">
  <data key="d0">Reserve Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reserve Force is typically deployed a short distance behind the main legion for strategic division.&lt;SEP&gt;A larger legionary body positioned several Prussian miles behind the Main Body to provide support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-089e96fcb6c53d4fe37413f70873aedd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Body">
  <data key="d0">Main Body</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The central core of the army which serves as the primary mass and foundation for the deployment system.&lt;SEP&gt;The Main Body represents the centralized portion of an army that follows the Advance Guard.&lt;SEP&gt;The Main Body relies on outposts for security against approaching enemies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Main Body refers to the central military force that relies on forward and side detachments for protection and information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b7b86e9f8571611dae96128b88d77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b9839be4f5c76a97ace71baf8a2625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffd9ee2ca6a2dbeb008f986d03860045</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flanks">
  <data key="d0">Flanks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The lateral sides of a military formation that are critical to protect against envelopment by the Enemy Forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e42e0d19c01d89b60bcea1e8c8214463</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774738</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
