<node id="Prussia">
  <data key="d0">Prussia</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Prussia is a historical state recognized for its strategic military contributions across the 18th and 19th centuries. During the era when Frederick the Great ruled, the state maintained a small territory while relying on efficient troop usage. Known formally under King Frederick II, Prussia led a kingdom that engaged in the Silesian Wars against Austria and its allies. Furthermore, this monarch guided Prussia into forming an alliance with Britain and Hanover opposing Austria, France, Russia, and Sweden.

Moving into the early 19th century, Prussia implemented significant military reforms which established the Landwehr system through specific government decrees and created the Landsturm organization. As a nation associated with the First Corps and a main army that required time to gather, Prussia actively participated in the general anti-Napoleonic wars. Its generals were prominent figures in these conflicts, including the period where Prussia joined the Seventh Coalition in 1815. At this critical juncture, Prussia contributed the Silesian Army under the command of Blücher. Through these various campaigns and structural changes, Prussia functioned as a historical state defined by its complex alliances and formidable military capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ea6ac7b39b9305030f2c7226a86db43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5bb89666881fe685b53314cebe1abaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f00c9046ba6740391ca82c677577b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfca00a9897a7d585d9175d5bc52771c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5caa7084b9aab1683b075dc4fc333250</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
