<node id="Fortress">
  <data key="d0">Fortress</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A fortress serves as protective boundary defining part of a Theater of Operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fortresses become strategic support points only when they are large enough to influence the broader area.&lt;SEP&gt;A Fortress is a fortified defensive structure that provides protection and deterrence when cantonment troops are positioned behind it.&lt;SEP&gt;Fortresses serve as defensive strongholds where critical supplies are stored, particularly within enemy territories.&lt;SEP&gt;Fortress represents fortified positions located near deployment sites and retreat routes to ensure defensive strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6ca1393bac88b8acf9da2a729f68294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-089e96fcb6c53d4fe37413f70873aedd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9577d681c513d8a72e8f9e09ad316f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77045b1c2599a8ac0acb0e781562ae49</data>
