</node>
<node id="Landsturm">
  <data key="d0">Landsturm</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Landsturm is a national militia force organized in Central and Western European nations.&lt;SEP&gt;Landsturm was a local militia form appearing in late 19th and early 20th century Central European nations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Netherlands">
  <data key="d0">Netherlands</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Netherlands was a country where the Landsturm militia was established.&lt;SEP&gt;The Netherlands served as the operational theater for the Anglo-Dutch Coalition during the 1794–1795 Winter Campaign.&lt;SEP&gt;The Netherlands refers to the lowlands area including present-day Holland, Belgium, Luxembourg, and part of northern France.&lt;SEP&gt;Region cited as an example where long-term warfare impacted the feasibility of supply systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Netherlands was granted formal independence from Spain, a right formally recognized by the Peace of Westphalia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22b58faf893c88031c709a0cfac971fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b03fbc1bc0a2f36813dfff78edd095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b9839be4f5c76a97ace71baf8a2625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ceef5e0b237a9edd2580a6c4fbfed04</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sweden">
  <data key="d0">Sweden</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Sweden was represented by Crown Prince Bernadotte, who commanded the Northern Army of the Coalition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sweden was a location where the Landsturm militia appeared.&lt;SEP&gt;Sweden was part of the coalition opposing France during the Grand Alliance War and later Prussia during the Silesian Wars.&lt;SEP&gt;Sweden was part of the alliance opposing Prussia in the Silesian Wars.&lt;SEP&gt;Sweden emerged as a strong Northern European power after acquiring important ports and territories from the Peace of Westphalia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f00c9046ba6740391ca82c677577b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b03fbc1bc0a2f36813dfff78edd095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5caa7084b9aab1683b075dc4fc333250</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Switzerland">
  <data key="d0">Switzerland</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Switzerland was a nation associated with the presence of the Landsturm militia.&lt;SEP&gt;The Swiss Confederation was formally recognized as an independent nation separate from the Holy Roman Empire by the Peace of Westphalia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b03fbc1bc0a2f36813dfff78edd095</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Russia">
  <data key="d0">Russia</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Russia has participated in notable international military alliances and developed unique internal structures throughout its history. Russia joined the Seventh Coalition formed in March 1815 to oppose France. Additionally, Russia was part of the alliance opposing Prussia in the Silesian Wars, participating alongside Austria and Sweden. Internally, Russia is identified as a nation retaining remnants of Tatar systems in its military and administrative structure. During specific eras, Russia is cited as a country practicing recruitment duties as taxes. Moreover, Russia is a region mentioned as practicing a government-funded military supply system alongside Hungary.

Regarding specific campaigns, the Russian campaign took place in this nation, characterized by severe supply constraints. The campaign ended in failure, largely attributed to the neglect of supply problems. The territory contested during the 1812 Campaign includes Moscow, Smolensk, and Borodino. While this vast territory where the Russian Army operated served as a potential base due to its size, the invaded territory was characterized by hostile environments for supply extraction. These factors combined to define the logistical challenges faced in Russia during the 1812 conflict.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ea6ac7b39b9305030f2c7226a86db43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f00c9046ba6740391ca82c677577b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22b58faf893c88031c709a0cfac971fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6725d3545cdb40e1dfdd2209aba40f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6e328b37fa2162a0fbd3f638331548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2a90ee6c570c1f41213848bde0e55e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfca00a9897a7d585d9175d5bc52771c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516f6a00a475faea10c611a860305297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5caa7084b9aab1683b075dc4fc333250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c8520f94840f0c06aabc2e77297761e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
