<node id="Silesia">
  <data key="d0">Silesia</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Silesia is a historical region that served as the primary territory contested between Prussia and Austria during the Silesian Wars. In December 1740, Silesia was attacked by Frederick II and became a significant battlefield, functioning as a province connected to Saxony through Frederick the Great's military movements that facilitated supply and troop positioning. The region is associated with a significant war that changed army deployment strategies and acts as an example regarding the limits of sustained supply sources over years of war. Throughout its history, Silesia was a region where multiple military operations and deployments occurred involving Frederick the Great and French marshals.

During 1813, Silesia operated as the deployment area for the Silesian Army commanded by Blücher. It was the operational region where Macdonald and Blücher encountered each other, engaging in operations involving distinct road divisions and army corps. Within this timeframe, Silesia was a region where Blücher conducted frequent maneuvers in 1813 involving multiple back-and-forth movements. Geographically and strategically, the territory served as the departure point for Austrian forces and the base for Prussian movements, solidifying its role as a central hub for conflicting military interests across different eras.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-85b7b86e9f8571611dae96128b88d77c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e5cd33cb23eede2329c705a877b7cf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2918db8fd4527a62709762ff6d5e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22b58faf893c88031c709a0cfac971fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c55a94307c751d0e9fbf6270e7773d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66ab621011ad683c952d4d1bfeab457d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e57f8d4f60b7c38f053668dcb48030cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5caa7084b9aab1683b075dc4fc333250</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774796</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
