<node id="Separated Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Separated Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Separated deployment involves dividing the main force into several parts based on specific distances, often temporarily due to situational requirements rather than intended independent operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battle Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Battle Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The objective of separated deployment is to eventually concentrate forces for a decisive battle; separating is viewed as a condition or last resort to achieve this goal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Range">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactics refer to deployments conducted with specific combat tasks, distinct from general deployment which lacks immediate combat orders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strategic Stage">
  <data key="d0">Strategic Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The strategic phase ends when the enemy approaches for a comprehensive battle, shifting focus entirely to the engagement moment.</data>
