<node id="Ney">
  <data key="d0">Ney</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ney was a French marshal who advanced through the Brandenburg Border alongside Oudinot without deploying a vanguard unit.&lt;SEP&gt;Ney is ordered by Napoleon to advance north and restrain the British forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8b814c286eb1e073648265d5177eb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ceef5e0b237a9edd2580a6c4fbfed04</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774807</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wellington">
  <data key="d0">Wellington</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Duke of Wellington commanded a separate corps in the same theater as Blücher in 1815.&lt;SEP&gt;Wellington commands the British army which Ney is tasked to constrain.&lt;SEP&gt;Wellington is an opposing commander whose forces concerned Napoleon alongside those of Blücher during the campaign.&lt;SEP&gt;Wellington is a military commander who poses a strategic threat to the attacking force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8b814c286eb1e073648265d5177eb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9577d681c513d8a72e8f9e09ad316f8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adfddc40b68714749a17f1f73f04abea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfca00a9897a7d585d9175d5bc52771c</data>
