<node id="Flank March">
  <data key="d0">Flank March</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Flank March requires familiarity with terrain and maintaining distance between columns.&lt;SEP&gt;Flank March is an alternative name for parallel marching, which alters the geometric positions of troop parts during movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Flank march involves changing the original perpendicular marching direction to the left or right side.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8b814c286eb1e073648265d5177eb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38f13e59336c7bb333fab6bbbe0ac097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a0950d107000f63848660e8ffc0706</data>
