<node id="France">
  <data key="d0">France</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">France is a European nation-state with a rich history of military engagement and strategic evolution. Originally entering the Thirty Years' War to weaken the Holy Roman Empire, France participated in the Peace of Westphalia, subsequently gaining significant power and influence as a result of the treaty. In the 18th century, France was a participant in the Grand Alliance War and the Silesian Wars, where it often opposed Prussia as part of alliances formed specifically to counter that power. By February 1, 1793, France declared war on the Anglo-Dutch Coalition, consisting of Britain and Holland, advancing military actions into the Netherlands region. During later campaigns, France faced invasions from the Sixth and Seventh Coalitions. It also served as the home country for the French Army fighting in the 1812 Campaign, associated with figures like Georges de Chambray, and remains the origin of the French Army referenced in contexts involving Valenciennes.

Strategically, France is noted for its historical reliance on cavalry as a primary weapon during the period described, although internal military conflicts occurred where cavalry composition varied, influencing historical perceptions of army structures. The nation adapted its military models by adopting the Horse Artillery unit system developed elsewhere. Furthermore, France exemplifies tactical challenges where troops suited for concentration had to disperse in foreign territory, such as Spain. Through these diverse campaigns and military adaptations, France maintained a critical role in European affairs, acting as both an aggressor and a defender against various coalitions while evolving its army structures over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3c6b62745fd7ff550d76846c1a46a8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed0edc361ac37e0deef9374d8ec557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f00c9046ba6740391ca82c677577b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-407ccaa628a42045b9ed85ea7bc4db1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2918db8fd4527a62709762ff6d5e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bace62a86e707c9881144ea59dde7a4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7f6e47322107075587da5b8dd1c7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6e328b37fa2162a0fbd3f638331548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b03fbc1bc0a2f36813dfff78edd095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b9839be4f5c76a97ace71baf8a2625&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ceef5e0b237a9edd2580a6c4fbfed04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516f6a00a475faea10c611a860305297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5caa7084b9aab1683b075dc4fc333250</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774814</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
