  <data key="d2">The Vanguard Unit is a specialized formation intended to lead the advance and protect the main force, usage varied between eras and commanders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774816</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outpost System">
  <data key="d0">Outpost System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Outpost System refers to the security measures and units deployed around a camp or march route, varying in complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774816</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brandenburg Border">
  <data key="d0">Brandenburg Border</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Brandenburg Border is a region in the north where Oudinot and Ney conducted military marches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frederick the Great's Army Size">
  <data key="d0">Frederick the Great's Army Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The recorded strength of Frederick the Great's army ranged between 30,000 and 40,000 personnel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Napoleon's Army Size">
  <data key="d0">Napoleon's Army Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The recorded strength of Napoleon's army ranged between 100,000 and 200,000 personnel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Changes">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Changes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The evolution of military tactics where armies function as composite bodies requiring detailed plans rather than simple commands.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68bce0e3733aefaac111940411ed6dd7</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encampment Area">
  <data key="d0">Encampment Area</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Encampment Area is a designated space for settling troops, designed with specific geometric shapes and positions relative to other formations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cantonment Troops">
  <data key="d0">Cantonment Troops</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Cantonment Troops are military units stationed in an encampment to secure territory and manage supplies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outpost Force">
  <data key="d0">Outpost Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Outpost Force is a unit tasked with monitoring the enemy and determining the size of the encampment area based on resistance time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Towns and Villages">
  <data key="d0">Towns and Villages</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Towns and Villages are settlements whose distribution influences the positioning of troops for encampment and deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Winter Cantonment">
  <data key="d0">Winter Cantonment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Winter Cantonment refers to a fortified encampment specifically established during the winter season for long-term stationing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marching Troops">
  <data key="d0">Marching Troops</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Marching Troops are mobile military units that set up encampments along their route rather than spreading out widely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stationed Troops">
  <data key="d0">Stationed Troops</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Stationed Troops refer to permanent military garrisons that maintain a fixed presence compared to mobile forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mounters Couriers">
  <data key="d0">Mounters Couriers</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mounted Couriers represent a reliable communication method used to transmit enemy intelligence after frontline resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beacon and Signal Flares">
  <data key="d0">Beacon and Signal Flares</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beacon and Signal Flares are visual signaling tools used by vanguards to communicate warnings, though less reliable than couriers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supply Region">
  <data key="d0">Supply Region</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Supply Region is an area targeted by the enemy for resource requisition, motivating the width of the encampment zone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frontier Defense Time">
  <data key="d0">Frontier Defense Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frontier Defense Time refers to the duration a vanguard can hold off the enemy, calculating available preparation time for cantonment troops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Straggler Elements">
  <data key="d0">Straggler Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Straggler Elements refer to non-combatants and supplies left behind in an encampment, such as sick soldiers and wagons, which constitute a security risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15f89854b5dda629cc5dcfc4edcef1c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\战争论.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778774817</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
