<edge source="Infantry" target="Cavalry">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Infantry possesses stronger independent combat capability than Cavalry, which relies heavily on external support for defense.&lt;SEP&gt;Infantry is considered the main branch while Cavalry serves a subordinate role in battle plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Infantry operations often depend on Cavalry support, creating a need for pre-planned integration to prevent confusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Cavalry and Infantry are assigned specific outer and middle routes in old battle sequences.</data>
